invariant: INV-16
file: widemul.h
catches: widemul_runtime_test
reason: widemul_p256_point_from_bytes inverts its branch, so the operation runs
  p256_wide_point_from_bytes, on the native 64x64->128 multiply, for every answer but
  WIDEMUL_CONSTANT_TIME, a wiped direction's 0 and WIDEMUL_NOT_STATED among
  them, and p256_point_from_bytes on the decomposition for the one answer
  that states the multiply's timing. Every byte still comes out the same.
  bin/widemul_runtime_test counts the calls into each copy and requires
  the wide files alone under the constant-time answer.

--- old
    if (widemul_native(widemul)) {
        return p256_wide_point_from_bytes(o, in);
--- new
    if (!widemul_native(widemul)) {
        return p256_wide_point_from_bytes(o, in);
